.Dd $Mdocdate: September 17 2026 $
.Dt CLI-GENERATED 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cli-generated
.Nd an example generated using the cli template
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm cli-generated
.Op Fl hVv
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Ar arg ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a template command line tool.
It logs to
.Em stderr
and prints a greeting to
.Em stdout .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar file
Specify an alternative configuration file.
.It Fl h
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl V
Print the version, git hash and build date, then exit.
.It Fl v
Produce more verbose output.
Once enables debug messages, twice enables trace messages.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width CLI_GENERATED_LOG
.It Ev CLI_GENERATED_LOG
Log filter in
.Sy env_logger
syntax, for example
.Ql debug
or
.Ql cli_generated=trace .
Takes precedence over
.Fl v .
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory of the default configuration file.
Defaults to
.Pa ~/.config .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ~/.config/cli-generated/config.toml -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/cli-generated/config.toml
Default configuration file, see
.Xr cli-generated.conf 5 .
.It Pa .env
Environment variables loaded from the current directory at startup.
Variables already set in the environment are not overridden.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print the version:
.Pp
.Dl $ cli-generated -V
.Pp
Run with trace output:
.Pp
.Dl $ cli-generated -vv foo bar
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cli-generated.conf 5
.Sh AUTHORS
.An your name Aq Mt author@example.com
